WEBVTT

00:17.600 --> 00:19.850
Better take this off for today.

00:24.590 --> 00:26.760
You peon! What are you looking at?!

00:27.100 --> 00:28.440
I'll kill you!

00:29.220 --> 00:30.800
Hey, Tachihara-kun.

00:30.800 --> 00:31.960
Nice seeing you here.

00:31.960 --> 00:35.340
Teruko-san managed to 
get Gilette to confess.

00:35.690 --> 00:40.990
You mean Jack Gilette of the 
Seventeen Worldly Evils?!

00:40.990 --> 00:45.920
I thought he would be a chew toy 
that would never fall apart!

00:45.920 --> 00:49.500
He broke in only half a year!

00:48.150 --> 00:49.810
I sympathize.

00:49.810 --> 00:51.400
With Gilette.

00:52.360 --> 00:57.560
Anyway, Tachihara-kun, thank you for your 
hard work on the infiltration mission.

00:57.560 --> 00:59.630
So, here's your new assignment.

01:00.340 --> 01:02.050
Deal with that problem.

01:02.050 --> 01:03.170
Carry me!

01:03.170 --> 01:04.590
I demand a piggyback ride!

01:05.500 --> 01:08.300
I'll start by summarizing the 
status of my investigation.

01:08.300 --> 01:09.070
Wee.

01:09.070 --> 01:11.920
Following the hostage crisis four days ago,

01:11.920 --> 01:15.090
we've determined that the infamous 
Decay of Angels was, in fact,

01:15.090 --> 01:17.360
the Armed Detective Agency.

01:17.360 --> 01:20.410
What are their goals?

01:20.410 --> 01:21.330
Any intel?

01:21.840 --> 01:26.230
The last sighting was the 
bank break-in two days ago.

01:26.230 --> 01:28.680
To think they'd raid a bank...

01:28.680 --> 01:29.900
Despicable.

01:30.660 --> 01:32.950
No training in the middle of a meeting!

01:34.110 --> 01:35.910
You're a perfect weight.

01:36.240 --> 01:39.390
Why haven't we had any further sightings?

01:39.390 --> 01:41.750
They must have already 
gotten what they wanted.

01:41.750 --> 01:45.500
The things a criminal on the run 
would want more than anything.

01:45.500 --> 01:48.490
A base and a command post.

01:45.500 --> 01:48.500
<b>Bungo Hound 
Dogs</b>

01:45.500 --> 01:48.500
<b>Episode 49</b>

01:50.000 --> 01:53.390
The goal of our mission is to prevent any 
terrorist attacks prior to the other side

01:53.390 --> 01:55.870
of the page being filled in, 
in addition to the recovery of said page.

01:56.770 --> 02:01.140
However, as wanted criminals,
 the Detective Agency can't act in plain sight.

02:01.670 --> 02:03.610
That's where her special ability comes in.

02:04.970 --> 02:08.310
By placing the two of you to Anne's Room,
 created by her ability,

02:08.310 --> 02:10.350
you will be able to infiltrate undetected.

02:10.770 --> 02:14.020
She will be the heart of our operation.

02:14.330 --> 02:15.980
You heard him.

02:15.980 --> 02:17.800
Well, tiger kitty?

02:17.800 --> 02:20.850
This ear's telling me it wants 
to hear you say thanks.

02:21.990 --> 02:22.910
Sorry.

02:23.650 --> 02:25.030
Why are you apologizing?

02:25.360 --> 02:27.220
For getting you mixed up in this.

02:27.220 --> 02:31.040
Cooperating with us right 
now is a serious crime.

02:31.410 --> 02:34.630
I don't think we can ever repay you enough.

02:34.630 --> 02:36.140
Why not?

02:36.140 --> 02:40.130
I'm the one repaying an impossibly 
huge debt right now, aren't I?

02:40.370 --> 02:41.030
Huh?

02:41.030 --> 02:41.630
Huh?

02:45.950 --> 02:47.040
Nothing! Nothing!

02:47.040 --> 02:48.000
Never mind that!

02:48.000 --> 02:50.130
Forget that! I'm begging you!

02:49.420 --> 02:50.710
It's time.

02:54.570 --> 02:55.590
Well, here we go.

03:08.170 --> 03:10.240
To the airport bus stop.

03:20.850 --> 03:23.740
Don't let anyone in until I say so.

03:23.740 --> 03:24.440
Yes, sir.

03:30.140 --> 03:33.910
I trust that you're ready, Fukuzawa.

03:33.910 --> 03:34.650
Yeah.

03:35.770 --> 03:37.020
<b><i>Tyrant</i></b>

03:38.700 --> 03:41.980
Why would our reunion be anything 
other than a drinking contest?

03:41.980 --> 03:44.870
You haven't changed, Gen'ichiro.

03:46.720 --> 03:47.990
What?!

03:47.990 --> 03:50.560
You still haven't gotten married?

03:50.560 --> 03:52.210
I'm busy with work.

03:52.540 --> 03:54.070
You stuck-up loner.

03:54.880 --> 03:57.330
I never would have thought you'd 
be the president, though.

03:59.090 --> 04:02.800
<b><i>Tyrant</i></b>

04:00.800 --> 04:02.790
But now that you are...

04:03.080 --> 04:04.510
you have responsibilities.

04:06.740 --> 04:08.550
Make your men surrender to the police.

04:09.080 --> 04:12.270
That way, the case will fall under 
the jurisdiction of the prosecution,

04:12.270 --> 04:14.750
and they will no longer be 
targeted by the Hunting Dogs.

04:14.750 --> 04:19.220
Because, so long as they are targeting you, 
they will never relent trying to tear you apart.

04:19.220 --> 04:21.950
I appreciate the concern, but...

04:22.600 --> 04:23.980
Bah.

04:24.310 --> 04:28.910
I suppose I might enjoy duking it 
out with you again like old times.

04:37.600 --> 04:39.180
Why did you stop?

04:39.180 --> 04:41.640
You aren't fooling me, Fukuzawa.

04:42.010 --> 04:47.340
You were going to make me cut your 
handcuffs and then swipe my sword.

04:48.550 --> 04:49.860
You got me.

04:50.720 --> 04:53.130
Fukuzawa, let's make a deal.

04:53.470 --> 04:56.850
You want to know what's 
happened to your Kunikida.

04:57.790 --> 04:59.810
Kunikida fell out of a helicopter 
and blew himself up.

05:00.430 --> 05:03.100
I know where he's gone.

05:05.890 --> 05:06.950
I don't need that.

05:08.030 --> 05:09.680
Kunikida is alive.

05:10.600 --> 05:16.070
If he were dead, 
I would definitely have sensed it.

05:20.100 --> 05:21.920
Well, shit.

05:22.180 --> 05:25.290
The lone wolf sure has changed.

05:26.890 --> 05:29.300
There's no way you are the greatest.

05:29.980 --> 05:31.210
Welcome.

05:31.210 --> 05:37.700
At the end of the day, your strength is 
the "I can beat up a ton of boars" kind,

05:37.700 --> 05:41.450
but the Hunting Dogs' job is 
investigating and arresting.

05:41.450 --> 05:42.140
So?

05:42.140 --> 05:45.500
So, I am the greatest hunting dog.

05:45.500 --> 05:46.760
You?

05:48.410 --> 05:50.240
I want to kill you <i>so</i> badly.

05:50.610 --> 05:51.910
Your order?

05:51.910 --> 05:53.010
Caffè latte.

05:53.010 --> 05:54.390
Soy sauce latte.

05:54.390 --> 05:55.560
Very good—

05:56.020 --> 05:57.240
Soy sauce?

05:57.240 --> 05:58.690
He'll have what I'm having.

05:59.170 --> 06:00.620
Let's make a bet.

06:00.620 --> 06:04.130
Whoever of us finds the Detective Agency's 
whereabouts first wins.

06:04.470 --> 06:05.590
You're on.

06:07.150 --> 06:10.420
Are the two of you with the police?

06:10.420 --> 06:11.100
Yes.

06:11.100 --> 06:13.430
We're investigating a case right now.

06:14.310 --> 06:18.450
Speaking of which, the heinous 
terrorist organization,

06:18.450 --> 06:22.910
the Armed Detective Agency, 
was right above this shop. Was it not?

06:22.910 --> 06:23.800
Yes.

06:23.800 --> 06:26.230
I saw them here on occasion.

06:26.920 --> 06:28.700
It's all so terrifying.

06:29.380 --> 06:30.280
Here you are.

06:31.270 --> 06:33.700
She's a waitress here, is she not?

06:34.010 --> 06:34.690
Yes.

06:34.690 --> 06:37.080
She's off work today.

06:37.910 --> 06:39.260
Do you need something from her?

06:39.960 --> 06:44.330
According to our information, 
she's very close with the Detective Agency.

06:45.560 --> 06:48.300
We suspect she's aiding their escape.

06:48.300 --> 06:52.830
They wouldn't get very far, 
depending on a low-level worker.

06:54.060 --> 06:55.630
Fantastic.

06:55.630 --> 06:58.710
I admire people who can make good coffee.

06:59.040 --> 07:03.080
I almost want you to come work 
at the commercial facility I own.

07:03.080 --> 07:05.700
There's only one problem.

07:05.700 --> 07:09.060
You're a dirty liar.

07:09.550 --> 07:10.870
Liar?

07:10.870 --> 07:13.280
I can tell from the sound of your breathing.

07:13.280 --> 07:18.450
You just said the Agency wouldn't get far,
 depending on a low-level worker.

07:18.890 --> 07:20.840
But that was a lie.

07:20.840 --> 07:23.530
You know of her special ability.

07:23.530 --> 07:26.260
I don't know what you're talking about.

07:26.820 --> 07:30.080
I understand you buy half a year's 
worth of beans at a time.

07:30.490 --> 07:34.180
Despite that, this coffee
 has such a fresh scent.

07:34.740 --> 07:36.010
How is that?

07:36.380 --> 07:39.470
It's because you stock your 
inventory in her room.

07:39.820 --> 07:42.580
Time can be slowed in a 
special ability space.

07:42.580 --> 07:45.450
You can keep a large quantity
 of beans fresh that way.

07:47.040 --> 07:48.700
Shall I continue?

07:49.080 --> 07:53.670
You just said Lucy-san has 
taken today off.

07:53.670 --> 07:55.200
That is also a lie.

07:55.530 --> 07:58.070
She's taken an indefinite break.

07:58.070 --> 08:00.710
She doesn't know if she can come back.

08:00.710 --> 08:03.430
Yet, you let her go.

08:03.430 --> 08:05.700
Because you understood

08:06.050 --> 08:09.660
that she's the only one who can 
save the Detective Agency.

08:09.660 --> 08:12.060
Now, here's the problem.

08:12.060 --> 08:15.310
You're an accessory to an act of terrorism.

08:15.310 --> 08:18.430
If, on top of that, you refuse 
to give up her location,

08:18.430 --> 08:21.610
you'll never make coffee again.

08:22.350 --> 08:23.340
Ow!

08:23.340 --> 08:24.650
Ow, ow, ow...

08:24.650 --> 08:26.280
What was that for?!

08:26.280 --> 08:30.840
You have a bad habit of tormenting people 
and taking pleasure in seeing them squirm.

08:31.850 --> 08:33.100
Boss...

08:33.610 --> 08:37.960
Is it wrong to want to repay 
someone you're dearly indebted to?

08:39.070 --> 08:42.970
I promise you, that if you 
tell us where she is now,

08:42.970 --> 08:45.200
she will not be questioned for any crimes.

08:45.980 --> 08:48.360
We have the authority to make that so,

08:48.360 --> 08:51.720
and a world in which a girl's
 honest intentions are rewarded

08:51.720 --> 08:53.780
is one that we ought to protect.

08:54.770 --> 08:58.760
It isn't just Lucy-chan 
that I want to be saved.

08:59.070 --> 09:00.380
The Detective Agency.

09:01.260 --> 09:05.380
I promise they'll be given a fair trial.

09:05.870 --> 09:07.220
Sheesh.

09:07.220 --> 09:09.430
I knew this would happen.

09:10.250 --> 09:16.470
I promise on my sword that, if our promise 
is broken, I will cut open my gut.

09:18.480 --> 09:19.440
Please.

09:20.620 --> 09:25.970
Lucy-chan said that she won't regret 
ruining the remainder of her life.

09:27.870 --> 09:31.300
Please save her future.

09:33.980 --> 09:35.200
I shall.

09:36.410 --> 09:40.710
She's gone to the Sky Casino.

09:42.290 --> 09:44.930
What a ridiculous construction.

09:45.410 --> 09:49.270
Most people believe that the civilian 
entertainment facility is just a front,

09:49.270 --> 09:52.860
and that it was really built by the winners 
of the war for surveillance and intimidation.

09:52.860 --> 09:55.580
It would be both a physical 
and political catastrophe

09:55.580 --> 09:58.820
if this place were to be attacked 
by terrorists or something.

10:04.040 --> 10:08.790
<b>Sky Casino 
General
 Manager


Sigma</b>

10:04.040 --> 10:08.790
<b>m 0 0 l 70 0 70 200 0 200</b>

10:04.040 --> 10:08.790
<b>(Real 
name
 unknown)</b>

10:04.040 --> 10:08.790
m 0 0 l 55 0 55 200 0 200

10:06.860 --> 10:08.790
Manager, we have a problem.

10:09.680 --> 10:11.010
Terrorists?

10:11.420 --> 10:12.330
That's right.

10:12.330 --> 10:14.950
There are terrorists in this facility.

10:15.330 --> 10:16.560
We have proof.

10:16.560 --> 10:18.090
Proof?

10:18.090 --> 10:19.760
Sir, look.

10:20.600 --> 10:22.780
That's one of the terrorists.

10:23.070 --> 10:26.860
She used her pocket dimension 
ability to bring them all in here.

10:26.860 --> 10:28.760
Then send a search team 
to scour the facility.

10:28.760 --> 10:29.760
It's no use.

10:30.170 --> 10:32.780
She can hide with them 
in the pocket dimension.

10:32.780 --> 10:34.110
What do we do, then?

10:34.630 --> 10:36.200
We close the casino.

10:36.200 --> 10:37.030
Refused.

10:37.380 --> 10:38.410
What?

10:38.410 --> 10:39.600
Bastard!

10:39.600 --> 10:41.380
Do you have any idea how serious this is?

10:42.300 --> 10:44.390
Of course I do.

10:47.660 --> 10:50.050
Those are directed resonance guns.

10:50.790 --> 10:53.590
They were made to combat Gifted.

10:53.590 --> 10:55.920
The sound waves affect the brain,

10:55.920 --> 10:59.930
causing loss of consciousness within 
one second and death within ten.

10:59.930 --> 11:01.880
Wanna try it out?

11:02.440 --> 11:04.500
You dare defy the government?

11:04.500 --> 11:05.650
The government?

11:06.110 --> 11:11.160
Under international law, this casino is
 outside the jurisdiction of any country's police.

11:11.160 --> 11:12.860
It's effectively an independent nation.

11:12.860 --> 11:15.040
Therefore, I am the law.

11:15.040 --> 11:17.740
If you want to spend your 
money here and leave, good.

11:17.740 --> 11:18.850
Otherwise...

11:18.850 --> 11:19.690
Get lost!

11:20.700 --> 11:22.730
How dare you!

11:22.730 --> 11:25.570
Did you just tell me to get lost?!

11:26.450 --> 11:28.700
Ah, shit.

11:29.400 --> 11:31.080
Okay!

11:31.080 --> 11:32.700
This area is secured.

11:33.980 --> 11:35.360
Wh-What the...?!

11:35.360 --> 11:38.130
Someone's blown up the landing zone!

11:38.130 --> 11:39.500
What?!

11:41.800 --> 11:44.730
No one's getting out of this casino now!

11:45.050 --> 11:47.630
We're going to split up 
and search the casino!

11:48.080 --> 11:50.970
You figure out what the 
Agency's next move is.

11:51.440 --> 11:52.880
Yes, sir.

11:54.520 --> 11:56.110
An explosion?!

11:56.110 --> 11:57.840
By terrorists?

11:57.840 --> 11:59.010
Stay calm.

12:00.400 --> 12:02.900
Our top priority is to keep 
our clients from panicking.

12:03.520 --> 12:06.700
Tell them it's an electrical failure and
 escort them to their hotel rooms.

12:07.090 --> 12:10.460
Client A4098, Lazarus, is unstable.

12:10.460 --> 12:12.200
Assign security to him in particular.

12:12.730 --> 12:15.320
Client E2988 has a 
chronic heart condition.

12:15.320 --> 12:16.920
Make sure the medical staff visit him.

12:17.470 --> 12:18.910
Wow...

12:18.910 --> 12:22.680
I heard he memorizes all of his clients' 
names and characteristics instantly.

12:22.680 --> 12:26.900
No wonder they say he was 
born to manage a casino.

12:27.490 --> 12:30.680
Such a mild incident will 
be forgotten by next week.

12:31.230 --> 12:35.190
If you understand, deal with it!

12:35.460 --> 12:36.340
Yes, sir!

12:45.570 --> 12:47.560
This couldn't have gone any worse.

12:47.560 --> 12:49.270
I should have kicked the Hunting Dogs out.

12:49.540 --> 12:52.260
They must be the ones behind the explosion,

12:52.260 --> 12:55.120
which means they're going to 
investigate the casino thoroughly.

12:55.120 --> 12:58.470
If they find out what 
this casino really is...

13:01.510 --> 13:03.170
I have to kill them.

13:04.760 --> 13:08.120
No evidence on this floor, either.

13:10.930 --> 13:11.950
What's that?

13:14.910 --> 13:16.150
A coin?

13:21.980 --> 13:23.640
The Detective Agency!

13:24.280 --> 13:26.600
That room is their hideout!

13:32.620 --> 13:34.730
I don't sense anyone here.

13:34.730 --> 13:37.680
They must have noticed me coming 
and escaped to the pocket dimension.

13:41.830 --> 13:43.510
The carpet has been cut.

13:44.310 --> 13:45.830
There's something under the floor.

13:50.500 --> 13:51.660
A safe?

13:54.200 --> 13:55.800
Metal manipulation.

14:09.430 --> 14:12.010
Currency from around the world.

14:12.010 --> 14:13.830
All in coins.

14:14.410 --> 14:16.280
H-How?!

14:16.720 --> 14:18.970
How have the Hunting Dogs found it?

14:19.410 --> 14:20.540
Impossible...

14:20.540 --> 14:24.470
Did he just manage to stumble into 
that particular unassuming room?

14:24.470 --> 14:26.130
S-Stay calm.

14:26.530 --> 14:28.980
Their communication devices and weapons

14:28.980 --> 14:32.010
were confiscated along with 
those of the other customers.

14:32.010 --> 14:35.840
Which means, if I kill them now, 
I can protect the secret.

14:37.060 --> 14:38.300
Sigma-san.

14:39.010 --> 14:42.050
I'll give you a word of advice,
 as a colleague.

14:42.050 --> 14:45.930
If you're found out by the Hunting Dogs
 in the middle of the mission...

14:45.930 --> 14:47.940
Abandon everything and run.

14:48.450 --> 14:50.830
You won't stand a chance.

14:52.040 --> 14:53.400
Abandon everything?

14:53.710 --> 14:55.380
The casino?

14:55.750 --> 14:57.190
Odd...

14:57.190 --> 15:00.130
Are these coins hollow?

15:00.130 --> 15:01.200
<i>No...</i>

15:01.200 --> 15:03.310
<i>There's something inside.</i>

15:03.310 --> 15:06.090
<i>Some kind of impurity 
in the metal structure.</i>

15:05.480 --> 15:06.830
I'm sorry.

15:17.490 --> 15:18.840
It's over.

15:19.800 --> 15:22.270
He can't have evaded instant 
death at that distance.

15:22.770 --> 15:25.290
A high-precision explosive 
disguised as a coin.

15:25.640 --> 15:28.730
It's the savage weapon at the 
center of the Decay of Angels'

15:28.730 --> 15:30.580
next worldwide terrorist attack.

15:31.110 --> 15:34.460
Now that they've seen it, 
I can't send them home alive.

15:36.080 --> 15:38.140
<i>That was close.</i>

15:38.140 --> 15:39.070
What?!

15:39.330 --> 15:42.140
I managed to stop the shrapnel 
with my special ability,

15:42.140 --> 15:44.190
but the blast knocked me down.

15:44.710 --> 15:47.800
Hang on, are all the coins 
in this safe bombs?

15:48.130 --> 15:49.550
I didn't finish him!

15:49.920 --> 15:50.980
Now what?!

15:51.520 --> 15:52.420
Wait...

15:53.070 --> 15:55.260
I still have my last resort,

15:55.770 --> 15:59.970
but it'll cause severe damage to the casino.

16:01.690 --> 16:03.970
You won't stand a chance.

16:04.400 --> 16:06.720
That may be true.

16:06.720 --> 16:10.020
Of the superhuman organization 
that is the Decay of Angels,

16:10.020 --> 16:12.550
I'm the one with the least combat ability.

16:13.070 --> 16:16.330
Outside the casino, I'm nothing.

16:17.160 --> 16:18.660
Wow...

16:18.660 --> 16:22.450
I heard he memorizes all of his clients' 
names and characteristics instantly.

16:22.450 --> 16:26.700
No wonder they say he was 
born to manage a casino.

16:27.590 --> 16:29.260
Everyone's got it wrong.

16:29.680 --> 16:31.480
I have no talent.

16:32.440 --> 16:34.930
I have to sacrifice sleep to memorize

16:34.930 --> 16:38.230
the clients' profiles and 
study the casino like crazy.

16:38.820 --> 16:41.380
I didn't want to lose the casino.

16:42.400 --> 16:45.010
Therefore, I...

16:47.450 --> 16:48.680
Are you serious?

16:49.820 --> 16:51.690
An unmanned aircraft?!

16:57.630 --> 16:59.040
<i>It's too big.</i>

16:59.360 --> 17:01.680
<i>I can't stop it with my 
metal manipulation ability!</i>

17:02.290 --> 17:03.750
Stand back.

17:04.250 --> 17:06.090
Weakling.

17:25.330 --> 17:27.960
It tried to challenge me in a sumo match.

17:27.960 --> 17:29.490
Silly airplane.

17:29.490 --> 17:31.340
Damn...

17:33.980 --> 17:35.350
You can't be serious.

17:35.690 --> 17:37.480
Haven't you done enough?!

17:38.140 --> 17:38.980
Tachihara!

17:56.500 --> 17:57.760
What was that?

17:57.760 --> 17:59.300
Another explosion?

18:02.490 --> 18:04.140
I see.

18:04.140 --> 18:06.040
Coin bombs.

18:06.040 --> 18:08.260
What an exhilarating display of evil.

18:08.870 --> 18:12.150
The customers take the 
coins out of the casino.

18:12.150 --> 18:15.510
Then, once they've been
 traded around the world,

18:15.510 --> 18:17.280
they'll all be triggered at the same time.

18:17.740 --> 18:20.880
This casino itself is a terrorist.

18:21.170 --> 18:25.500
So that's why that manager was 
in such a hurry to kick us out.

18:27.640 --> 18:30.200
This is where the trigger 
signal is transmitted from.

18:31.010 --> 18:34.960
A signal from such a high altitude 
would reach across the world.

18:35.210 --> 18:36.260
What do we do?

18:36.860 --> 18:38.980
We take the central communication room

18:38.980 --> 18:41.840
and expose the casino's 
plans to the entire world.

18:48.240 --> 18:52.400
Are you lot that desperate to dance with me?

18:54.110 --> 18:55.520
I hear fighting.

18:56.950 --> 18:58.540
The Hunting Dogs are on the move.

18:59.490 --> 19:02.790
And that is the Decay of Angels' next plan.

19:03.220 --> 19:06.530
A global act of terrorism, targeting 
all humanity indiscriminately.

19:06.870 --> 19:10.210
But their true goal is the 
panic that will ensue.

19:10.630 --> 19:15.220
Currency, the basis of a 
state's trust, will kill people.

19:15.450 --> 19:19.450
Never mind a great depression, 
it could trigger the next world war.

19:20.140 --> 19:23.390
This is the worldwide terrorism that
 the Decay of Angels will perform

19:23.390 --> 19:25.430
before they fill in the other side of the page.

19:25.940 --> 19:27.640
That much is certain.

19:28.410 --> 19:30.850
As the first step in stopping 
this terrorist attack,

19:30.850 --> 19:33.540
we'll have the Hunting Dogs 
discover the coin bombs

19:33.540 --> 19:35.440
and take control of the comms room.

19:36.050 --> 19:40.140
By working with the Hunting Dogs 
to stop a terrorist attack,

19:40.140 --> 19:42.480
we'll prove that we aren't terrorists.

19:43.010 --> 19:46.250
And we capture Sigma, 
who knows where the page is,

19:46.250 --> 19:48.000
as a member of the Decay of Angels.

19:48.980 --> 19:51.200
That's Dazai-san's plan.

19:52.780 --> 19:55.160
This is the Hunting Dogs' combat power...

19:55.760 --> 19:57.890
This is what it means to 
be in a different league.

19:58.400 --> 20:04.170
But us nothings have our 
own way of fighting!

20:06.330 --> 20:09.600
Why did you choose Sigma 
to protect the casino?

20:09.600 --> 20:11.750
What are you talking about?

20:11.750 --> 20:13.570
Are you really going to play dumb?

20:13.570 --> 20:18.560
I discovered something interesting 
when I looked up this Sigma man.

20:19.070 --> 20:24.660
His life began when he was arrested 
by European police three years ago.

20:25.760 --> 20:27.610
He has no past.

20:28.360 --> 20:32.690
He's like a novel that starts 
halfway through the story.

20:33.860 --> 20:36.400
All I learned was his special ability.

20:36.400 --> 20:41.550
The ability to trade, with anyone he touches, 
the information each person wants most.

20:41.910 --> 20:46.470
He used that ability to steal the 
location of the page from Chief Taneda,

20:46.470 --> 20:50.010
but you only needed him for that instant.

20:50.440 --> 20:53.450
So why did you leave him 
in charge of the casino?

20:53.450 --> 20:55.480
Why do you think?

20:55.810 --> 21:00.280
I don't think he's even a 
terrorist to begin with.

21:00.280 --> 21:03.520
It's said that the Sky Casino was 
built following a secret meeting

21:03.520 --> 21:06.520
of the victors of the war thirteen years ago,

21:06.940 --> 21:10.640
but no intelligence organization 
had information about it.

21:10.640 --> 21:16.830
That's when I realized: the Sky Casino 
wasn't built thirteen years ago.

21:17.370 --> 21:18.890
It was built eight days ago.

21:19.700 --> 21:23.820
It emerged instantaneously, having been written 
about on the page eight days ago,

21:23.820 --> 21:26.390
along with thirteen years' worth of history.

21:27.880 --> 21:29.810
I'll go back to my first question.

21:29.810 --> 21:32.960
Why did you assign Sigma to the casino?

21:32.960 --> 21:35.630
Because he's the most powerful of all.

21:35.630 --> 21:36.800
Powerful?

21:36.800 --> 21:40.070
Who do you think is the 
strongest in the world?

21:40.520 --> 21:41.820
Gifted?

21:41.820 --> 21:43.180
Political leaders?

21:43.180 --> 21:44.690
Nope.

21:45.470 --> 21:49.770
The most powerful man is the 
man who has nothing else.

21:51.980 --> 21:54.740
Sigma doesn't have a past.

21:55.200 --> 21:57.530
He has amnesia.

22:01.650 --> 22:05.470
Sorry, but guns don't work on me.

22:05.470 --> 22:06.170
Fall back!

22:06.170 --> 22:07.520
Retreat for now!

22:10.450 --> 22:11.770
Teruko-san!

22:12.180 --> 22:13.390
Are you all right?

22:14.510 --> 22:15.510
Tachihara...

22:16.640 --> 22:21.280
The heroes of justice are gonna 
go save the world wounded.

22:21.280 --> 22:24.270
Don't you think this makes for 
quite the exhilarating picture?

22:24.610 --> 22:27.120
<i>It's the injury from when 
she stopped the plane.</i>

22:28.110 --> 22:30.030
What was that noise?

22:30.030 --> 22:31.360
The security guards are on the ground.

22:31.360 --> 22:32.430
Shit...

22:33.840 --> 22:35.910
Is something wrong?

22:35.910 --> 22:37.310
Not to worry.

22:37.310 --> 22:38.610
I'm with the police.

22:39.000 --> 22:40.990
We're currently investigating 
some terrorists.

22:40.990 --> 22:43.240
This floor is safe.

22:43.240 --> 22:44.110
Oh.

22:44.110 --> 22:45.470
I'm glad to hear.

22:47.560 --> 22:48.630
What?!

22:51.830 --> 22:52.760
Tachihara!

22:54.520 --> 22:56.770
Now we don't have to pay for our losses!

22:56.770 --> 22:57.960
Honey, wait!

22:59.130 --> 23:00.320
<i>Attack!</i>

23:00.320 --> 23:04.180
<i>I repeat: attack these two on sight.</i>

23:04.180 --> 23:05.610
<i>You won't be accused of any crime.</i>

23:06.410 --> 23:09.490
<i>Your gambling losses will be erased.</i>

23:09.830 --> 23:11.770
<i>You'll earn ten thousand dollars 
for any injury inflicted on them.</i>

23:11.770 --> 23:13.490
<i>One million dollars if you kill them.</i>

23:18.830 --> 23:22.990
Unsure of who he was, 
Sigma looked for a place to be.

23:22.990 --> 23:25.170
That place was the casino.

23:25.430 --> 23:32.060
This is why he'll torch the Hunting Dogs 
with hellish tenacity to protect the casino.

23:33.250 --> 23:36.010
The most terrifying thing of all...

23:36.020 --> 23:40.010
Next Episode: 50

23:36.770 --> 23:39.630
is a mediocre man who is desperate.
